# TEMPLATE for the T5 scope sweep (spec `.totem/specs/seed20-apparatus-slice2.md` § S6).
#
# `src/t5-sweep.mts` substitutes __PACKAGE__ with the lowered policy's package name
# and writes the result to `rego/build/<subdir>/<pkg>/t5-sweep.rego`, then evaluates
# it beside the PUBLISHED `artifacts/lowered/<pkg>/policy.rego` in ONE `opa eval`.
#
# WHY A SET, NOT AN OBJECT. The emitted `in_scope` is a partial rule with NO
# `default` (`src/lower.mts` § Lowering 5), so a path the policy does not match
# leaves it UNDEFINED rather than false. In an object comprehension an undefined
# value silently drops the key, and the artifact would show a shorter map with no
# indication that anything had been dropped. In a set comprehension "dropped" IS the
# reading: membership means in scope, absence means out of scope, and the two are
# recovered from one list.
#
# WHY ONE EVAL. `data.__PACKAGE__.in_scope with input as {"file": p}` re-binds the
# whole document per path inside a single evaluation, so 2,742 paths cost one
# process start instead of 2,742. The per-path form is exercised too — on a sample —
# so the batched reading is checked against the form it replaces rather than trusted.

package t5sweep

import rego.v1

in_scope_paths := {p |
	some p in input.paths
	data.__PACKAGE__.in_scope with input as {"file": p}
}
